  "text": "What do you want to be when you grow up? A doctor, a lawyer, a surgeon, a CEO, some big, bright company? No? A poet, an artist, an actor, a star, sweetheart? No. None of these things you are. You are what we want we want you greedy. See me? See how good I'm doing? A pet of a company, our profit margin moving up to the trillions, while the numbers of the starving are in the millions, but at least I'm not one of them. What do you want to be when you grow up? And don't tell me something stupidly creative. We've got something to generate that for us. No need for you or anything you do, unless you're sitting in an empty room, a chair, a desk, a company laptop. What do you want to be? Anything but me, sweetheart, has to be the wrong answer.",
